e Kirkland, a Republican focused on agriculture and water policy, advanced from the crowded primary but has struggled to fund his campaign, holding under $20,000 in cash in the fall against Costa's roughly $940,000.\n\nRaters across the spectrum place the race between Likely D and Solid or Safe D, and prediction markets give Costa roughly 94 to 97 percent odds. No public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, ratings, and the money gap. An underfunded challenger against a well-established incumbent makes an upset difficult to construct, though the district's only modest Democratic lean leaves room for the race to tighten.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9726, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.957, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9737, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9821, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9693, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9851, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9724, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9732, "margin": 14.5}]}